2fgu|n|One of the common people; a vulgar person. ; The vernacular, or common language.	N:2gzx,56,2~2gzx,56,2
2fgu|a|Of or pertaining to the mass, or multitude, of people; common; general; ordinary; public; hence, in general use; vernacular. ; Belonging or relating to the common people, as distinguished from the cultivated or educated; pertaining to common life; plebeian; not select or distinguished; hence, sometimes, of little or no value. ; Hence, lacking cultivation or refinement; rustic; boorish; also, offensive to good taste or refined feelings; low; coarse; mean; base; as, vulgar men, minds, language, or manners.	j:1nl0,89,4;18tz,64,4;2gzl,56,2;2gzx,56,2~18tz,64,4;1nl0,89,4;2gzl,56,2;2gzx,56,2
